# Magic Garden - gameplay loop, transcribed from the original (UFO 50 #5, bgm27_gameplay).
# 44 bars x 8 rows, 11 frames a row (an eighth note at 163.6 BPM). tools/song.py documents the format.
# First draft by tools/draft_gameplay.py; edited by hand from here on. The lead (bars 0-23, 40-43) was re-derived from
# the original's octave-stack signature, row by row, with its echo notes and dynamics.

song song_gameplay
speed 11

# The original's lead is an octave stack (f, 2f, 4f at 0/-1.4/-5 dB, almost no odd harmonics): the 12.5 % pulse
# is the closest duty. It holds ~40 ms and decays ~1 dB per 20 ms (-15 dB by the end of the row): env=-1.
# Echo notes and the outro's crescendo use the same sound at lower volumes (instruments 4-7).
duty  1 lead  duty=12 vol=15 env=-1
duty  2 chord duty=50 vol=8  env=-2     # a stab that is gone in about a row and a half
duty  3 pad   duty=50 vol=13 env=-2     # C section stabs on CH2: two stab notes alternate where there are two
duty  4 lead12 duty=12 vol=12 env=-1
duty  5 lead9  duty=12 vol=9  env=-1
duty  6 lead6  duty=12 vol=6  env=-1
duty  7 lead3  duty=12 vol=3  env=-1
duty  9 pbass duty=50 vol=15 env=0      # C section bass on CH1 (the wave channel plays the melody there)
wave  1 bass  vol=100 wave=0
wave  2 flute vol=100 wave=1 cycles=4    # C section melody: the original's near-pure whistle tone (every overtone under -25 dB)
wave  4 flute3 vol=100 wave=3 cycles=3   # the same tone from a 3-cycle wave, for the notes its period grid tunes better
wave  3 hush  vol=100 wave=2 cycles=4    # the melody's rests: a flat wave at the sines' average level. Cutting or muting the wave
                                        # channel drops its output from ~7.5 to 0 and thumps; this keeps the level
waveform 0 8BEFECA989999877 88876666765310 14   # one bright cycle: sounds an octave below the note table, reaching G1
waveform 1 9BB964469BB964469BB964469BB96446   # four sine cycles at half height; its strays (7f, 9f) stay above 11 kHz here
waveform 2 77777777777777777777777777777777   # silence at the sines' mean (7.5): rests without a DC step
waveform 3 9BBB9744468ABBA8644569ABB9754457   # three sine cycles at half height, strays under -30 dB (plus the fixed image at 9.7f)
# The melody sits at the original's octave (E6-A7), two octaves over the stabs: an octave lower it lands on their
# upper harmonics, masks them and turns its G#/C# against their G into a harsh rub. It is balanced like the
# original, level with the stabs (half-height waves; the C-section pad and bass turned up). Each note uses the
# 4-cycle or 3-cycle wave whose period grid is closer: all within 8.5 cents, every stray above 11 kHz.

